    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.basics\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI’d personally prefer the toggles occur at the global level (`set` instead of `setlocal`). An option to determine which level is used for all toggles would be great. Even better if this could be configured per-toggle but I think that might not be worth the effort.",
