        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nIndeed, 'mini.basics' has overall design of being as much \"plug and play\" as possible. Yet I don't think having this kind of configurability in this case is worth it.\r\n\r\nMoreover, I'd like to encourage users to move away from parts of 'mini.basics' that they want to precisely customize (it is [more or less mentioned in help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ccfc6300a5c17387f2899f979ecc04f942bee2a0/doc/mini-basics.txt#L32-L35)). So my suggestion would be to creating your own mappings that use `:set` following [this part of source code](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ccfc6300a5c17387f2899f979ecc04f942bee2a0/lua/mini/basics.lua#L613-L638). If you want only part of mappings to use `:set` you can create them after `require('mini.basics').setup()` to override only part of them.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
